{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 5, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "## Lost in Translation (and Loving It!) - A Whirlwind Trip to Japan\n\nJapan. The word itself conjures images of ancient temples, neon-lit streets, and serene gardens. And let me tell you, the reality is even more captivating! I just returned from a week exploring this incredible country, and I’m already dreaming of going back.\n\nMy journey started in Tokyo, a dazzling metropolis that seamlessly blends tradition and modernity. I wandered through the vibrant Shibuya crossing, marvelled at the colourful Harajuku fashion, and found moments of peace in the Meiji Jingu Shrine. The food scene was, unsurprisingly, phenomenal. From slurping down ramen to indulging in delicate sushi, every meal was a delight.\n\nNext, I took the Shinkansen (bullet train!) to Kyoto. This city felt like stepping back in time. I explored stunning temples like Kinkaku-ji (the Golden Pavilion) and Kiyomizu-dera, and strolled through the enchanting Arashiyama Bamboo Grove.  Wearing a traditional kimono and wandering the Gion district, hoping to catch a glimpse of a geisha, was a truly magical experience.\n\nBeyond the iconic sights, it was the small moments that really stood out: the impeccable politeness of the people, the meticulously crafted gardens, the quiet reverence in temples.  Navigating the language barrier was sometimes challenging, but always part of the adventure! \n\nJapan is a feast for the senses, a culture rich in history and beauty. It’s a place that stays with you long after you’ve left.  Highly recommend adding it to your travel bucket list!\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "##", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": "▁Lost", "logprob": -0.0011177966371178627}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": -1.7787781953811646}, {"token": "▁Translation", "logprob": -0.0005864569102413952}, {"token": "▁(", "logprob": -1.9102468490600586}, {"token": "and", "logprob": -0.00022110